Sources: jemoic-openharmony-code-source OpenHarmony_5.0_release
  - User_source_code/mwv207_mesa.patch (video-codec/, 56 files, ~10.6k lines)

Porting steps (all verified by hardware tests):
1. video-codec/ tree extracted from the patch (new files)
2. meson: video sources + inc dirs wired into baseline driver meson
3. context.c: hook mwv207_context_video_codec_init()
4. winsys drm.h: install enhanced version (ENGINE/RELOC/BO_ACC macros)
5. winsys.h: MWV207_DEBUG_* flag bits (MWV207_DEBUG_VIDEO)
6. resource.h: MWV207_RESOURCE_FLAG_{VIDEO_BUFFER,SUBALLOC} names
7. PIPE_TIMEOUT_INFINITE -> OS_TIMEOUT_INFINITE (24.x API)
8. FIX: mwv207_video_buffer get_resources was NULL — vaGetImage
   (frame readback) crashed in vlVaGetImage; implemented
   mwv207_video_buffer_resources() (mirrors vl_video_buffer.c)

Results (Deepin 25, kernel 6.6.143, in-tree mwv207 KMD, env-only):
  vainfo: H264 CB/Main/High/High10 + HEVC Main/Main10 + VideoProc
  ffmpeg 1080p H264 hw decode: CPU utime 2.060s -> 0.367s (17.8%)
  frame readback pixel-validated for both H264 and HEVC
